            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Human pride, rebellion against God, systemic idolatry, and an oppressive, worldly anti-God system or empire.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Genesis 11:1-9\",\"Revelation 14:8\",\"Revelation 17:1-18\",\"Revelation 18:1-24\",\"Daniel 4:28-30\",\"Isaiah 13:1-22\",\"Isaiah 14:4-23\",\"Jeremiah 50:1-46\",\"Jeremiah 51:1-64\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"The first-century Roman Empire, functioning as a cipher for state-sponsored persecution of Christians (Preterist and Early Church view).\",\"basis\":[\"1 Peter 5:13\",\"Revelation 17:9\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The Roman Catholic Church or papal system (Historicist and classical Protestant Reformer view).\",\"basis\":[\"Revelation 17:4-9\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"A literal future rebuilt city of Babylon on the Euphrates River functioning as the center of the Antichrist's end-times empire (Dispensational Futurist view).\",\"basis\":[\"Revelation 17:1-18\",\"Revelation 18:1-24\",\"Zechariah 5:5-11\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"First-century apostate Jerusalem, judged for persecuting the prophets and apostles and rejecting Christ (some Preterist views).\",\"basis\":[\"Revelation 11:8\",\"Revelation 18:24\",\"Matthew 23:34-37\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"There is nearly universal consensus on Babel/Babylon's broad thematic symbolism as a representation of human pride, idolatry, and a worldly society opposed to God's kingdom. However, eschatological debates fracture considerably over the specific historical or future referent of 'Babylon the Great' in the Book of Revelation.\"}",
